 ["CB19", "2026-06-18", "(bake + cb_12seed)", "FINAL: bake combined defaults (chi_r=0.85, p_r_inf=1.0, p_2inf=0.5, s_ddot-drop default-on)", "baked so COMBINED_BARRIER=1 gives 25/25 OOTB", "FINAL CONFIG BAKED"],
 ["CB20", "2026-06-18", "cb_12seed", "12-seed noisy (5x5x12=300) on the drop config", "205/300 SP (68%), 268/300 land, worstResid 5.3 -- looks noise-fragile; the 3-seed 75/75 was optimistic", "noise picture needs context (CB21)"],
 ["CB21", "2026-06-18", "cb_vs_bm", "NOISE: combined-barrier vs BACK-MAPPED, 4 hard cells x 6 seeds", "combined 16/24 BEATS back-mapped 13/24; far less breach (2.83 vs 19.29) -- the SEN G_s^-1 starvation is worse under noise", "NOT a noise regression -- combined-barrier comparably-to-MORE robust"],
 ["CB22", "2026-06-18", "cb_sddot_kept/tuned", "KEEP s_ddot: hard-cap (DH_D_CAP), tau-LPF (CB_SDDOT_TAU), SG-clean (CB_SDOT_FILT)", "ALL worse than drop: cap2 still un-lands IC5; SG-clean DIVERGES (full s_ddot magnitude over-drives); tau0.8 best at 5/6", "keep-s_ddot strictly worse than drop"],
 ["CB23", "2026-06-18", "cb_filt_noisy", "Savitzky-Golay s_dot filter (causal quadratic least-squares) under noise", "16/24 UNCHANGED across W=0/9/13 (worstResid 2.83->2.58 only) -- s_dot is NOT the dominant noise path; the measured flow h is", "SG filter kept as gated option; not the noise fix"],
 ["CB24", "2026-06-18", "cb_peraxis/asym/rectify/other_gains", "s_ddot-KEPT per-axis tuning: chi_r=[1.1,0.65] + rectifiers", "22/25, breaches: Circ IC4 NEEDS chi_r_x>=1.1 (precision) but chi_r_x>=1.1 destabilizes Static/Liss IC3 (Y-breach, X-tilt cross-couples to Y); NO p_2inf/E/chi_r_y rectifies", "light-s_ddot wall; reduce chi_r_x next"],
 ["CB25", "2026-06-18", "cb_skept_redux/07/cont/t15", "KEEP s_ddot via HEAVY LPF: reduce chi_r kills divergence; tau=1.5 + chi_r=0.85", "reduced chi_r=0.7 STABLE(21/25 no breach); full s_ddot still diverges; Gamma_x diverges; tau=1.5 removes 1/z spike keeps smooth target-accel FF -> chi_r climbs to 0.85 -> 25/25 SP + 74/75 noisy, no breach", "KEEP-s_ddot reaches 25/25 via heavy tau1.5; BUT see CB29 (damped cycle, not converged)"],
 ["CB26", "2026-06-18", "cb_ztaper* (REVERTED)", "z-taper: scale s_ddot by min(1,alt_above/z_ref) -> cancel 1/z terminal over-drive, NO lag", "low tau=0.5 + z_ref=2.0 -> 24/25 noiseless + 75/75 noisy, no breach; responsive FF fixes Liss IC3 noisy miss. BUT uses ALTITUDE", "INVALID: scale-free/unknown-depth premise -> reverted to commit a152479"],
 ["CB27", "2026-06-19", "cb_lt_peraxis/traj", "Per-axis + terminal-phase trajectory: WHY do low-tau cells fail?", "NOT offset/lag -> FORCED LIMIT CYCLE: lateral osc ~1Hz +-0.1m/+-0.3m/s locked to |h_d_lat| 0.07->0.6; touchdown catches random phase. Residency LOW (interior, not funnel-limited)", "failures are a forced under-damped cycle, not a tunable offset"],
 ["CB28", "2026-06-19", "cb_damp/sens/cap/flowfilt", "Lever exhaustion: which control param damps the velocity cycle?", "NONE. chi_r damps position-amp not velocity (forcing-set); p_r/p_2inf/cap(no bite)/gamma_2/E/N/kappa flat or diverge; optical-flow filter CB_SDOT_FILT partial-damp but lag diverges fast cell (Liss IC3), never SP; h_d filter wrong point (drop keeps h_d, no cycle)", "velocity amplitude is s_ddot-FORCING-set; only filter the forcing (lag) or drop"],
 ["CB29", "2026-06-19", "cb_traj_cmp", "Does heavy-tau converge or limit-cycle? vs drop terminal trajectory", "heavy-tau = DAMPED cycle ~0.25 (not converged, passes by phase luck); DROP more damped ~0.16 -> more margin -> 75/75 vs 74/75; s_ddot FF re-injects cycle energy even at tau1.5", "DROP is the scale-free OPTIMUM (most damped); heavy-tau = drop+leftover forcing"],
 ["CB30", "2026-06-19", "cb_root", "Root of the underlying cycle (present even in drop)", "under-damped lateral loop: sigma_x osc +-0.14 but |sigma|<<E=1.0 ALWAYS -> switching linearized away -> no nonlinear damping; eR~0.15rad > commanded tilt 0.10rad -> INNER-LOOP attitude lag (cascade-bw mismatch)", "root = inner-loop attitude lag suspected; kR/kOmega + E test PENDING"],
 ["CB31", "2026-06-19", "cb_kr_asym/kx_finish", "Inner-loop speedup on responsive keep-s_ddot: kR/kOmega up, then per-axis kR split", "kRx2 KR=[3;3;0.5] KOmega=[0.6;0.6;0.1] + tau0.7 -> 17/25->24/25 no breach (only Liss IC3 vel0.273). ASYMMETRIC kR_y<3 is a DEAD END: 'fixes' Liss IC3 only by detuning into another limit-cycle basin (sharp Hopf bistability; ky2.0 damped, ky2.25 pumped 0.41) but FULL 5x5 breaks Static IC3/IC5 + Circ IC4/IC5 -> 18-19/25; 6-cell probe missed collateral", "kR raises stability margin (helps) but cycle persists; asymmetric kR illusory"],
 ["CB32", "2026-06-19", "cb_tau_finish", "Heavy tau at symmetric kR=[3;3;0.5] (collateral-free lever)", "tau 0.9->24/25, tau1.0->24/25, tau1.2->25/25, tau1.5->25/25 (no breach, worstResid0.618). Liss IC3 0.27->0.12. Deterministic 25/25 keeping responsive s_ddot -- but see CB33/CB34 (phase luck)", "deterministic 25/25 via heavy tau -- NOT a real fix"],
 ["CB33", "2026-06-19", "cb_noisy_resp", "NOISY validation of the responsive tau1.2 25/25 config, 4 seeds x 5x5", "83/100 SP (seeds 25,25,24,9), 96/100 land, worstResid 2.014 (FUNNEL BREACH). Liss IC3 vel jumps 0.066->1.452(sd3)->3.781(sd4). Deterministic 25/25 -> fragile under noise", "responsive tau config NOT bakeable -- phase-fragile"],
 ["CB34", "2026-06-19", "cb_cause/phase/lag_probe", "MECHANISM: is tau damping the cycle or its effect? Measure the FF's damping sign", "FF magnitude is BOUNDED ~0.4 (capped, NOT 1/z-exploding). corr(-FF_x,vx)=+0.64 KEEP vs -0.50 DROP -> s_ddot FF is ANTI-DAMPING (injects power in phase with velocity, mean(FF*vx)=+0.044>0). Net corr(a_actual,vx)=-0.02 KEEP (~zero net damping=sustained) vs -0.18 DROP (decays). tau sweep: corr(-FF,vx) +0.77(0.5)->0.00(1.5) ONLY by attenuating FF toward zero; no tau keeps FF AND healthy damping. FF intrinsic positive-feedback on ego-velocity (h=v/z)", "ROOT = FF anti-damping cancels natural damping. DROP (remove FF) is the UNIQUE complete elimination -- restores -0.18 damping -> cycle decays. 25/25+75/75. Drop default stands"],
 ["CB35", "2026-06-19", "cb_keep_noisy", "KEEP s_ddot directive: noise-validate the tau where FF stops anti-damping (tau1.5, corr=0); CB33 only tested tau1.2", "tau1.5 (and 1.8): noiseless 25/25 but NOISY 83/100 -- seeds 1,2 clean, seeds 3,4 blow up Liss IC3 (2.0,3.8), breach 2.09. Removing the NOISELESS anti-damping is not enough: net damping only -0.04 (vs drop -0.18) -> noisy s_ddot FF re-excites the barely-damped cycle. No tau saves keep-s_ddot under noise", "keep-s_ddot is noise-fragile at EVERY tau; needs ADDED damping, not just de-anti-damping"],
 ["CB36", "2026-06-19", "cb_asym_diag/koy/koy_noisy", "WHY asymmetric kR fails + find a compensating param (user directive, keep s_ddot)", "Asymmetric kR=[3;2;0.5] fails MIXED-axis: Static/Linear on X (0.20-0.26), Circ on Y (0.28-0.31); Liss IC3 itself bistable. Compensator = kOmega_y=0.10 (LOW Y attitude-rate gain detunes the Y resonance; p2inf_y nearly irrelevant, 0.35 vs 0.50 both work) -> FULL 5x5 25/25 noiseless, no breach (resid 0.610), KEEPING s_ddot. BUT NOISY 85/100 -- seed4 Liss IC3->5.22, breach 1.51, 21/25 land. Same wall as CB33/CB35", "per-axis gains (kR_x, kOmega_y, p2inf_y) RELOCATE the resonance to deterministic 25/25 but DON'T add net damping -> can't beat the ~83-85/100 noise wall. Robust keep-s_ddot needs explicit added damping (e.g. scale-free flow-damping -k_d*h), not gain redistribution"],
 ["CB37", "2026-06-19", "cb_param_damp", "WHICH control param reduces the cycle? One-at-a-time sweep on Liss IC3, metric = netDamp corr(a_actual,vx) + terminal pp(vx) (cycle itself, not pass/fail)", "Ranked by net damping (keep s_ddot, baseline netDamp=-0.02): chi_r=0.5 -> -0.28 (STRONGEST), kR_xy=4 -> -0.18 (= DROP ref), DROP -0.18. NON-levers: kOmega_xy & E_xy only shrink amplitude (netDamp~0); raising Gamma_xy/gamma2/chi_r=1.2 DIVERGES (boundary-layer destabilize); default kR_xy=1.5 diverges keep-s_ddot. Consistent w/ CB10 (chi_r0.5) + CB30 (kR damping route)", "ONLY chi_r(lower~0.5) and kR_xy(raise~4) add net damping while keeping s_ddot; chi_r strongest. Both have global tradeoffs (chi_r0.5 costs Circ precision CB11; kR4 over-damps CB18) and neither alone beats the noise wall -> combine for margin"],
 ["CB38", "2026-06-19", "cb_combine_damp/seed4_diag/p2z", "COMBINE the two damping levers (chi_r-lower + kR_xy-raise) vs noise wall; per-axis decompose the residual; add descent-axis lever", "Symmetric stack chi_r=0.65 kR_xy=4 keep-s_ddot: noiseless 25/25 no breach -> NOISY 89/100 (seeds1-3 PERFECT 25/25, up from 83-85 wall; seed4=14/25). Per-axis decomp of seed4: the wall is DESCENT(vz)-DOMINATED -- ~8 cells fail pure-vz~0.20 (noise inflates terminal descent 0.10->0.20), only 2 are lateral-LC catastrophes (Liss IC3 vx1.06/vy2.08 breach 1.70; Static IC5 vz2.09). Added P2INF_Z_OVERRIDE hook (test-only, default p_2inf(3)=1.5 unchanged); tighten 1.5->1.0 = vz margin -> 92/100 (seed4 17/25), 0.7 no better. Residual = Liss IC3 lateral divergence (noise-excited), gain-margin tuning can't remove", "stacked damping + descent-margin: keep-s_ddot 83->89->92/100. chi_r-low+kR-high makes 3/4 seeds perfect; descent lever P2INF_Z=1.0 best. Remaining wall = noise-excited Liss IC3 lateral divergence; still < drop 75/75-equiv robustness"],
 ["CB39", "2026-06-19", "cb_push_liss/liss_trace/p20/yaw_perf", "PUSH the residual seed-4 Liss IC3 breach (chi_r_x-lower, early flow funnel p_20-lower); TRACE the cycle; YAW perf check", "(1) chi_r_x LOWER backfires: [0.55;0.65]->81, [0.50;0.65]->78 (de-weights zeta_r -> noise-fragile, regresses other cells); chi_r=0.65 is the noise floor. kR_x>4 over-stiffens (CB37). (2) TRACE Liss IC3 seed4: cycle IGNITES AT ALTITUDE (vy->1.84 @4m, t=1.5s), rotates X<->Y (coupled 2-D mode), partial mid-descent recovery, then terminal divergence (|v|2.6, breach@t3.54). NOT terminal-margin -- a noise-ignited GROWING oscillation = the s_ddot anti-damping pump under worst-case seed. (3) p_20_xy tighten DOES kill it (seed4 2.76->0.19 @p_20=14!) but over-constrains all else -> 65/100; tighter breaches on IC offset. (4) YAW HEALTHY: noiseless terminal |e_a|<2.5deg all cells, bounded |u_a|<1.6, kappa_a<0.24 (peaks are IC3 initial-acquisition transients); on diverging seed4 yaw dragged to 27.8deg but u_a/kappa_a stay bounded -> yaw is a VICTIM of the lateral cycle, not a cause", "92/100 is the keep-s_ddot CEILING: residual is suppressible only by global over-constraint (p_20=14 fixes Liss IC3 but wrecks 65/100). Yaw not implicated. Confirms only DROP removes the pump cleanly"],
 ["CB40", "2026-06-19", "cb_funnel_cause", "WHY does p_20-tighten kill Liss IC3 but wreck the rest? Measure flow-funnel OCCUPANCY (|V_h_e|/p_2) -- is it containment or gain?", "NOT containment: legit flow error |V_h_e_xy|=0.18-1.13 -> funnel occupancy only 0.01-0.10 at p_20=25; even the Liss IC3 seed4 DIVERGENCE peaks at |V_h_e|=2.39 = occupancy 0.20. The flow error NEVER nears the funnel. Real mechanism: barrier gain G_2 = (e^z2+1)^2/(2 e^z2 p_2) ~ 1/p_2 -> p_20 is covertly a LOOP-GAIN knob. Tightening raises flow-loop gain everywhere: enough authority to damp Liss IC3's s_ddot pump, but into the cascade lag it over-drives the other cells (p_20=14 noiseless breach resid1.48 is a POSITION breach from over-aggressive control, not a flow breach; monotone worse 10->5.9). Same gain-vs-lag tradeoff as Gamma/gamma2 (CB37)", "UNIFIES the keep-s_ddot campaign: residual = authority/damping deficit curable only by raising loop gain (p_20/Gamma/kR/chi_r all gain knobs), but cascade phase-lag caps global gain -> no single gain damps Liss IC3 AND keeps the lag-limited cells. Structural no-free-lunch. Only DROP escapes (nominal gain already has +damping margin w/o the pump)"],
 ["CB41", "2026-06-19", "cb_seed4_z", "Re-identify the 8 failures of the 92/100 config (all on seed 4): per-axis + cause classify", "Split 5 DESCENT / 3 LATERAL -- the s_ddot pump acts on the Z axis too, not just laterally. TWO divergences on DIFFERENT axes: Static IC5 = DESCENT blow-up (vz=2.19 breach 1.10; IC5=[2,2,-3] low start -> vertical s_ddot 1/z-inflated ignites) -- earlier mislabeled lateral; Liss IC3 = LATERAL blow-up (vx/vy=2.76 breach 1.91). Plus 6 marginal: 4 descent vz~0.19-0.22 (p2inf_z=1.0 reduced but didn't kill), Sin IC3 lateral 0.53, Circ IC4 lateral 0.29", "92/100 residual is a TWO-AXIS s_ddot pump (lateral AND descent), descent the larger share (5/8). Beating it needs +damping margin on BOTH loops simultaneously -- cascade-lag-capped gain (CB40) can't do that globally. Reinforces: only DROP escapes"],
 ["CB42", "2026-06-19", "cb_zdamp/zfix", "WHICH gain removes the Z (descent) limit cycle? Added Z-SMC override hooks (GAMMA_Z/E_Z/CHIZ/GAMMA2_Z/KAPPA0_Z, test-only); netDamp(az,vz) sweep + full-noisy validate", "On Static IC5 seed4 (descent DIVERGENCE vz->2.19) baseline netDamp=+0.45 (strongly anti-damped). Only Gamma_z(descent sliding gain) reduces it (+0.45->+0.19 @3.0), then gamma2_z-low (+0.29) and chi_z-low (+0.37) -- but NONE crosses to net-damped, all still diverge. Full-noisy: Gamma_z=2.5 BREACHES noiseless (22/25 resid1.5) -- raising descent gain into the descent-loop lag (I_a_cd LPF tau0.08 + s_ddot_z pump) over-drives = same gain-vs-lag wall (CB40); gamma2_z=0.1->84 (worse), chi_z=0.012->91 (~same)", "NO control gain robustly removes the Z cycle while keeping s_ddot. Gamma_z is the right DIRECTION (descent damping lever, analogue of lateral kR) but gain-capped -- destabilizes before it damps. Confirms two-axis structural ceiling: s_ddot pump corrupts BOTH loops, neither escapes gain-vs-lag. Only DROP gives nominal Gamma_z=0.75 a +damping margin"],
 ["CB43", "2026-06-19", "cb_zclass", "WHY each Z gain fails -- classify by mechanism on a BOUNDED noiseless descent cycle (Static IC5): netDamp + authority std(a_z) + vz freq", "Several Z gains DO reach net damping noiseless: kappa0_z=0.5 (-0.24), E_z=0.3 (-0.07, freq 0.10->0.30=stiffness), p20_z=2 (-0.09), chi_z=0.10 (+0.12=integral). Gamma_z=3 does NOT damp (+0.49) -- authority EXPLODES std(a_z) 0.1->5.0 (chatter). Each damping mechanism becomes a NOISE LIABILITY: Gamma_z=chatter/over-drive; kappa0_z=adaptive-gain RUNAWAY on funnel breach (documented kappa_z runaway, N_z 0.05->0.02); E_z=hard-switching chatter; chi_z=integral WINDUP during divergence; p20_z/gamma2_z=G2 gain over-drive + lost terminal bound", "ROOT: descent surface sigma_3 = zeta_2(3)+chi_z*int has NO direct vz-damping term -> damping must be SYNTHESIZED via switching/stiffness/integral/funnel gain, each of which amplifies the noisy 1/z flow + s_ddot pump as much as the damping. Same knob that quiets the clean cycle ignites the noisy one (chatter/windup/runaway/over-drive). No Z gain survives to net damping under noise"],
 ["CB44", "2026-06-19", "cb_zcombo", "How to control kappa_z runaway + can a COMBINATION of descent gains tune it? Pair damping lever (kappa0_z) with anti-runaway (KAPPA_MAX_Z cap + leakage P_z); added P_Z_OVERRIDE hook", "kappa ODE: dk/dt=Theta_norm*N*G*|sigma| - N*P*k; drive explodes on breach (G2,|sigma|->big), leakage N*P=0.1 too weak. CONTROL: cap (KAPPA_MAX_Z) + raise P_z DOES bound it -- cap0.4+P_z20 cut worstResid 1.905->1.307 (lowest of any keep-s_ddot cfg), no catastrophic blow-up. BUT SP 92->86: capping low enough to stop runaway STARVES legit descent authority the marginal cells need (same kappa is both the runaway AND the needed gain -> confirms MT2 clamp-0.5-didnt-fix). COMBINATIONS (kappa0_z.5+cap+P_z+Gamma_z) all 86-90/100, none beats simple 92", "kappa_z runaway IS controllable (projection cap + leakage) but it is a SYMPTOM of the breach (s_ddot pump), not the cause -> bounding it doesnt recover SP. Combinations dont escape: descent levers are COUPLED through the same authority-vs-lag / damping-vs-runaway constraint (kappa damps AND runs away; capping kills both). No combo relaxes the constraint -> 92/100 keep-s_ddot ceiling stands; only DROP removes the forcing"],
 ["CB45", "2026-06-19", "cb_smooth/descent_cause/drop4", "SMOOTH DESCENT: which param removes/bounds the Z cycle? + FAIR drop-vs-keep over 4 seeds", "BOMBSHELL: Static IC5 seed4 descent blows up (peak|vz|~2.0, land=0) under EVERY config -- keep, cap+P, DROP, all kR(1.5-4)/chi_r(.65-.85)/p2inf_z(1-2.5) -> NOT the s_ddot pump, NOT tunable; a PATHOLOGICAL noise seed (unrecoverable descent transient, needs perception/flow-outlier handling). FAIR 4-seed comparison: baked DROP = 82/100 (seeds 25/25/24/8) vs keep-s_ddot 92-config = 92/100 (25/25/25/17). The drop '75/75 strictly better' was a SEED ARTIFACT (CB16 used seeds 1-3 only; seed4 never tested). Over the hard 4-seed set keep-s_ddot stacked-damping BEATS drop. Seeds 1-3 descend SMOOTH (peak|vz| 0.5-0.66) in all configs", "MAJOR CORRECTION: keep-s_ddot (chi_r=0.65,kR=4,p2inf_z=1.0,KAPPA_MAX_Z+P_z) is NOT worse than drop -- it WINS over 4 seeds (92 vs 82). Smooth descent IS achieved on all recoverable seeds by chi_r-low+kR-high+p2inf_z margin (+kappa cap backstop). The lone residual (Static IC5 seed4) is a noise outlier beyond ANY control gain incl drop -> perception-layer problem, not control"],
 ["CB46", "2026-06-19", "cb_s5_trace/cbf_audit", "Static IC5 seed4 REAL failure mechanism (signal trace) + CBF performance audit across runs", "MECHANISM (trace, DROP to isolate): descent guidance des h_z=-0.42 const -> demands vz=0.42*z (~1.2m/s @3m, aggressive, SHARED by all configs = h_rd setpoint). Descent under-damped -> vz OVERSHOOTS profile (vz1.28 vs des0.66 @z1.57). TRIGGER @t2.1 (altGap1.5m): measured optical flow h_z SIGN-FLIPS -0.39->+0.42 (gross perception error, 1/z-amplified pixel noise at high vz). Controller trusts it -> cuts thrust 20->2.9 + leans 30deg tilt (robs vertical thrust) -> vz runaway 2.1, no land. NOT s_ddot pump (drop fails too), NOT kappa_z runaway (kz stayed 0.22-0.34), NOT funnel (occ<0.27). It is a PERCEPTION failure (flow outlier) -> no control GAIN fixes it (all consume the bad measurement). Fix upstream: flow innovation/outlier gating, gentler h_rd, or velocity-aware flow (matches PERCEPTION_FLOW_FINDINGS ~2m/s range). CBF AUDIT: cbf_ok ~100% all runs, ~0%% hard-clamp, never saturates; actual tilt overshoots cone <=9deg on IC3 acquisition (absorbed by 15px inset); visibility HELD on all successes; CBF not implicated in any failure (Static IC5 s4 tilt 30deg still cbf_ok)", "Static IC5 seed4 = PERCEPTION (flow sign-flip outlier) + aggressive h_rd, NOT control -> perception-layer fix only. CBF performs correctly throughout (feasible ~100%, inset absorbs tilt overshoot, not a failure source)"],
 ["CB47", "2026-06-19", "cb_loom/pinvtol/pinvtol2/tol_cycle", "REAL cause of the h_z sign-flip + user lever pinv(L_s,TOL) 2nd-arg tuning + why low tol fails rest (limit cycle)", "h_z(loom) recovered by pinv(L_s,4)*dPdt; vz column of L_s=[-x;-y], loom is the WEAKEST singular mode. LOOM TRACE Static IC5 s4: pinv under-reports true h_z (err+0.20) then SIGN-FLIPS at featRad>1.2 (marker fills/overflows FoV near ground, NOT centering); corr(featRad,|err|)=+0.85. CAUSE = tol=4 TRUNCATES the weak loom SV (an SV sits in (1,4]). pinv TOL is a real lever: tol<=1.5 RETAINS loom -> Static IC5 s4 LANDS (peak|vz| 2.1->1.19). BUT global tradeoff: tol4=92/100 S5s4 blows up; tol1.5=88 S5s4 lands; tol0.01=44 (15/25 even NOISELESS). WHY rest fail (LIMIT CYCLE confirmed, Lis-IC4 noiseless): low tol UN-REGULARIZES pinv -> tiny SV divides finite-diff/quant error in dPdt -> loomErr 0.03->0.29 (10x) -> descent vz pp DOUBLES 0.70->1.57, freq DOUBLES 0.17->0.33Hz -> fail. Regularization-vs-resolution (truncated-SVD/Tikhonov) tradeoff", "pinv TOL = regularization knob on the ill-conditioned loom mode. High tol regularizes (clean, no cycle) but loses loom where critical (S5s4 runaway); low tol resolves loom (fixes S5s4) but amplifies error -> descent limit cycle on the rest. SAME wall, perception layer. REAL fix = well-conditioned loom measurement (direct apparent-size/area rate), NOT a tolerance value. Added PINV_TOL + loom-diag log hooks (test-only)"],
 ["CB48", "2026-06-19", "(loom root-cause: cb_loom/sv/pinvtol)", "DESCENT root cause: V_h(3) loom = vz/z FLOW DIVERGENCE, recovered as the 3rd row of pinv(L_s)*dPdt; vz column of L_s=[-x;-y] is the WEAKEST singular mode (sigma_min~2.09, in (0.01,4] 93%% of steps)", "pinv(L_s,TOL) tol=4 TRUNCATES the loom SV -> h_z under-reports + SIGN-FLIPS near ground (Static IC5 s4 descent runaway). tol<=1 RETAINS it (fixes S5s4) but un-regularizes -> amplifies dPdt finite-diff error -> descent LIMIT CYCLE (Lis-IC4 noiseless: vz pp/freq DOUBLE) -> suite 44/100. Regularization-vs-resolution (truncated-SVD) tradeoff; no single tol wins. SG-derivative dPdt to cut noise = fatal LAG (0/25)", "loom failure = ill-conditioned pinv weak-mode, NOT noise per se. Fix = estimate loom WITHOUT pinv (area-rate divergence). gyro can't de-rotate (target rotates) but AREA is rotation-invariant (curl+shear area-preserving) -> loom decoupled"],
 ["CB49", "2026-06-19", "cb_momverify/momval/calib", "SCALE-FREE moment loom: V_h(3) = -1/2 d(ln M)/dt, M=2nd-moment corner spread (fractional rate -> size/depth-invariant, fixed 1/2, no cal). Gated USE_MOMENT_LOOM (default off)", "VERIFIED vs analytical truth: slope 0.90-0.99 CONSISTENT across cells (=scale-free), corr 0.86-0.98. CALIBRATION beats pinv loom esp noisy (corr 0.918 vs 0.865, RMS 0.049 vs 0.062). CLOSED-LOOP keep-s_ddot 92-config: noiseless 25/25 (no regression) -> NOISY 92->95/100, breach 1.91->1.49. Residual = pre-existing pathological seeds (Static IC5 s4, Liss IC3 s4), NOT loom-caused", "moment area-rate loom is the validated win: better-calibrated + noise-robust + scale-free + decoupled (no sigma~2). 95/100. Opt-in via USE_MOMENT_LOOM=1; baked default unchanged"],
